      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1892 and stayed open until 1943, marking the town’s early communication hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machias%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Seattle, Lake Shore and Eastern Railway crossed Machias in 1888, linking it to regional trade routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
